-- title:
--   Order on the second branch versus the ideal (varpi,y,xⁿ)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a level $N\neq 0$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $red:A\to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two Hecke degeneracy embeddings $\bar\alpha,\bar\beta$ at level $N$, $q$, a place specialisation $P$ for these data, and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Assume $q\nmid N$, that $R$ satisfies `IsModel` (the two divisor laws together with the cusp laws at the $\infty$- and $0$-sides) and `OrderLawFixed` (at affine geometric places fixed by the square of the geometric Frobenius on places, the pushforward of the divisor of $f$ under `reduceFst` equals $\operatorname{ord}_v$ of the first residue plus $\operatorname{ord}$ of the second residue at the Frobenius translate), and that for a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, all supersingular (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set), the regularity and node-value laws hold. Let $K\subset\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be a number field, $w\in W$, and suppose every $a\in k$ with $a^{q^2}=a$ lies in the image of $A\cap K\to k$ induced by $red$. Let $c=(x,y)$ be node coordinates at $w$ over $K$, i.e. elements of the node ring $S:=$ `R.nodeIntegersOver K w` with first residue of $x$ zero, $\operatorname{ord}$ of the second residue of $x$ at the arithmetic-Frobenius translate $\varphi\cdot w$ equal to $1$, second residue of $y$ zero, and $\operatorname{ord}_w$ of the first residue of $y$ equal to $1$. Let $\varpi\in A\cap K$ be such that an element of $A\cap K$ reduces to $0$ in $k$ exactly when it is a multiple of $\varpi$. Then for every $g\in S$ and every natural number $n$: the second residue `nodeResidue₂` of $g$ at $w$ is zero, or its order at $\varphi\cdot w$ is at least $n$, if and only if $g$ lies in the ideal of $S$ generated by the constant $\varpi$, by $y$ and by $x^n$.
--
--   This is the saturation (normal-crossing) statement for the node ring at a supersingular point: vanishing to order $n$ along the branch cut out by the second reduction is detected by membership in the ideal $(\varpi,y,x^n)$, the case $n=0$ being the already available criterion for vanishing of the second residue. It is used in the construction of presentations of the node ring by inertia-fixed node coordinates.
